    <DataNode elementId="PHOSPHATIDYL-MYO-INOSITOL-45-BISPHOSPHA" textLabel="a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 4,5-bisphosphate" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="24742074" dataSource="PubChem-compound" />
      <Graphics centerX="500" centerY="1380" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment>The phosphorylated derivatives of |FRAME: L-1-phosphatidyl-inositols &quot;phosphatidylinositol&quot;| (PtdIns), collectively called phosphoinositides (PIs), are eukaryotic cell membrane phospholipids whose inositol head group is phosphorylated at position D3, D4, or D5, singly or in all combinations, to yield seven PI metabolites. The seven phosphoinositides found in animals include: Phosphatidylinositol monophosphates: |FRAME: CPD-177|, |FRAME: CPD-1108| and |FRAME: 1-PHOSPHATIDYL-1D-MYO-INOSITOL-5-PHOSPHA|. Phosphatidylinositol bisphophosphates: |FRAME: 1-PHOSPHATIDYL-1D-MYO-INOSITOL-34-BISPH|, |FRAME: 1-PHOSPHATIDYL-1D-MYO-INOSITOL-35-BISPH|, and |FRAME: PHOSPHATIDYL-MYO-INOSITOL-45-BISPHOSPHA|. Phosphatidylinositol trisphophosphate: |FRAME: PHOSPHATIDYLINOSITOL-345-TRIPHOSPHATE|. |FRAME: PHOSPHATIDYL-MYO-INOSITOL-45-BISPHOSPHA| is present at the plasma membrane and is a key regulator of actin remodelling and endocytosis, in addition to its role as a precursor to second messengers |CITS: [18774718]|. It recruits and/or regulates several proteins that are implicated in the first step of endocytosis, including the clathrin adaptor complex AP-2 and the large GTPase dynamin |CITS: [12119359]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="PHOSPHATIDYL-MYO-INOSITOL-45-BISPHOSPHA" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Chebi" value="18348" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Seed" value="cpd12582" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Metanetx" value="MNXM67" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_LigandCpd" value="C04637" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pubchem" value="24742074" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="a phosphatidyl-myo-inositol 4,5-biphosphate" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="PtdIns(4,5)P&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1&apos;-myo-inositol-4&apos;,5&apos;-bisphosphate" />
      <Property key="Synonym_4" value="PIP2" />
      <Property key="Synonym_5" value="phosphatidylinositol-4,5-bisphosphate" />
